repository-code: "https://github.com/skeisuke1977/xpsloss"
abstract: >-
  xpsloss implements oscillator energy-loss functions, causal dielectric response,
  and bulk inelastic scattering in Python. For normal emission, it calculates the
  fixed-depth effective XPS cross section including surface, vacuum, core-hole,
  and interference terms, for gapless materials and accepted materials with a
  hard band gap, and its average over single-scattering paths with an
  externally supplied constant weight length.
keywords:
  - X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy
  - dielectric response
  - electron energy loss
